<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>AI Summer Camp - Task 5</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/task5.css">
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@300;400;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.4.0/css/all.min.css">
</head>
<body>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="task-card">
            <!-- Header Section -->
            <div class="header-section">
                <a href="/lobby" class="back-btn">
                    <i class="fas fa-arrow-left"></i>
                    Back to Lobby
                </a>
                <a href="/logout" class="logout-btn">
                    <i class="fas fa-sign-out-alt"></i>
                    Logout
                </a>
            </div>

            <div class="task-header">
                <h1 class="task-title">Step 1: Natural Language Processing Challenge</h1>
                <p class="task-subtitle">Learning how AI understands human language and sentiment</p>
            </div>

            <!-- Introduction Section -->
            <div class="intro-section">
                <h2 class="section-title">From Numbers to Words: The Language Revolution</h2>
                <div class="intro-content">
                    <div class="intro-text">
                        <p class="description-text">
                            As AI advanced beyond recognizing patterns in numbers and categories, scientists achieved a remarkable 
                            breakthrough: teaching computers to understand <strong>human language</strong>. This meant AI could 
                            now draw patterns not just between classes or numerical values, but within the complex world of 
                            <span class="highlight">speech and text</span>.
                        </p>
                        <p class="description-text">
                            This field, called <strong>Natural Language Processing (NLP)</strong>, allows AI to analyze the meaning, 
                            emotion, and intent behind words. One of the most practical applications is <span class="highlight">sentiment analysis</span>—
                            determining whether text expresses positive, negative, or neutral feelings. This powers everything from 
                            social media monitoring to customer feedback analysis.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Training Data Section -->
            <div class="training-section">
                <h2 class="section-title">Step 1: Learn to Identify Language Features</h2>
                <p class="section-subtitle">Analyze these customer reviews to understand how AI detects sentiment through word patterns</p>
                <div class="training-grid">
                    <div class="training-item positive-review">
                        <h3 class="item-title">Positive Sentiment</h3>
                        <div class="review-icon">
                            <i class="fas fa-smile"></i>
                            <span class="sentiment-label">Happy Customer</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="features-list">
                            <h4 class="features-title">Customer Review:</h4>
                            <p class="review-text">"I absolutely <strong>loved</strong> this product! The quality is <strong>fantastic</strong> and it works <strong>amazingly</strong> well."</p>
                            <h4 class="features-title">Key Language Features:</h4>
                            <ul class="features">
                                <li><strong>Positive words:</strong> loved, fantastic, amazingly</li>
                                <li><strong>Enthusiastic tone:</strong> "absolutely loved"</li>
                                <li><strong>Praise language:</strong> "works well"</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="training-item negative-review">
                        <h3 class="item-title">Negative Sentiment</h3>
                        <div class="review-icon">
                            <i class="fas fa-frown"></i>
                            <span class="sentiment-label">Unhappy Customer</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="features-list">
                            <h4 class="features-title">Customer Review:</h4>
                            <p class="review-text">"I was so <strong>disappointed</strong> with this. It <strong>broke</strong> after only a week, and the customer service was <strong>terrible</strong>."</p>
                            <h4 class="features-title">Key Language Features:</h4>
                            <ul class="features">
                                <li><strong>Negative words:</strong> disappointed, broke, terrible</li>
                                <li><strong>Problem focus:</strong> mentions failures</li>
                                <li><strong>Critical tone:</strong> dissatisfaction expressed</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Testing Section -->
            <div class="testing-section">
                <h2 class="section-title">Step 2: Classify These New Reviews</h2>
                <p class="section-subtitle">Use your understanding of language features to determine sentiment</p>
                
                <div class="testing-grid">
                    <div class="test-item">
                        <div class="review-icon mystery">
                            <i class="fas fa-question"></i>
                            <span class="sentiment-label">Unknown Sentiment</span>
                        </div>
                        <label for="answer1" class="test-label">Review A</label>
                        <div class="features-list">
                            <p class="review-text">"The product arrived quickly and was easy to use, but the battery life is surprisingly short."</p>
                            <p class="observed-features"><strong>Your Analysis:</strong></p>
                        </div>
                        <select id="answer1" class="answer-select">
                            <option value="">Choose sentiment...</option>
                            <option value="Positive">Positive</option>
                            <option value="Negative">Negative</option>
                            <option value="Mixed">Mixed</option>
                        </select>
                    </div>
                    <div class="test-item">
                        <div class="review-icon mystery">
                            <i class="fas fa-question"></i>
                            <span class="sentiment-label">Unknown Sentiment</span>
                        </div>
                        <label for="answer2" class="test-label">Review B</label>
                        <div class="features-list">
                            <p class="review-text">"Outstanding quality! This exceeded all my expectations and I highly recommend it to everyone."</p>
                            <p class="observed-features"><strong>Your Analysis:</strong></p>
                        </div>
                        <select id="answer2" class="answer-select">
                            <option value="">Choose sentiment...</option>
                            <option value="Positive">Positive</option>
                            <option value="Negative">Negative</option>
                            <option value="Mixed">Mixed</option>
                        </select>
                    </div>
                    <div class="test-item">
                        <div class="review-icon mystery">
                            <i class="fas fa-question"></i>
                            <span class="sentiment-label">Unknown Sentiment</span>
                        </div>
                        <label for="answer3" class="test-label">Review C</label>
                        <div class="features-list">
                            <p class="review-text">"Worst purchase ever. Complete waste of money and doesn't work at all. Avoid this product!"</p>
                            <p class="observed-features"><strong>Your Analysis:</strong></p>
                        </div>
                        <select id="answer3" class="answer-select">
                            <option value="">Choose sentiment...</option>
                            <option value="Positive">Positive</option>
                            <option value="Negative">Negative</option>
                            <option value="Mixed">Mixed</option>
                        </select>
                    </div>
                </div>
                
                <div class="submit-section">
                    <button id="checkButton" class="submit-btn">
                        <span>Analyze Sentiment</span>
                        <div class="btn-icon">
                            <i class="fas fa-search"></i>
                        </div>
                    </button>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Feedback Section -->
            <div id="feedback" class="feedback-section hidden">
                <h3 class="feedback-title">Your Results</h3>
                <div id="score-display" class="score-display"></div>
                <ul id="feedback-list" class="feedback-list"></ul>
                
                <!-- Educational Explanation -->
                <div id="explanation" class="explanation-section">
                    <h4 class="explanation-title">What Just Happened?</h4>
                    <p class="explanation-text">
                        You just performed <strong>sentiment analysis</strong> using Natural Language Processing! Instead of 
                        analyzing numbers or simple categories, you examined the emotional tone and meaning within 
                        <span class="highlight">human language</span>. This is one of AI's most sophisticated capabilities.
                    </p>
                    <p class="explanation-text">
                        <strong>Natural Language Processing (NLP)</strong> allows AI to understand text by identifying key features 
                        like positive/negative words, emotional intensity, and contextual meaning. The AI doesn't just look for 
                        individual words—it analyzes patterns, combinations, and linguistic structures to determine overall sentiment.
                    </p>
                    <p class="explanation-text">
                        In real-world applications, NLP powers chatbots, virtual assistants, language translation, content moderation, 
                        and social media monitoring. Companies use sentiment analysis to understand customer feedback, track brand 
                        reputation, and improve their products based on what people are actually saying.
                    </p>
                    <p class="explanation-text">
                        What makes NLP remarkable is that it bridges the gap between human communication and machine understanding. 
                        By teaching AI to process language, we've enabled computers to interact with us in our most natural form 
                        of expression—words, sentences, and conversations.
                    </p>
                </div>
                
                <div class="next-section">
                    <button id="nextButton" class="next-btn">
                        <span>Complete AI Journey</span>
                        <div class="btn-icon">
                            <i class="fas fa-trophy"></i>
                        </div>
                    </button>
                </div>
            </div>

        </div>
    </div>

    <script src="/js/task5.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
